WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:14.619
- Hi, I'm Hannah,

00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:16.406
your friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:16.406 --> 00:00:17.641
and if you're anything like me,

00:00:17.641 --> 00:00:19.536
you believe that a glass of wine at 8 PM

00:00:19.536 --> 00:00:20.916
makes you a better mom.

00:00:20.916 --> 00:00:23.364
So pour yourself a glass
and let's talk about stuff.

00:00:23.364 --> 00:00:24.827
Tonight we're drinking

00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:28.160
some really fancy rosé, because why not?

00:00:29.241 --> 00:00:30.074
Wine not.

00:00:32.853 --> 00:00:34.096
Here's why I'm drinking tonight,

00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:36.773
my youngest son just started daycare.

00:00:36.773 --> 00:00:38.473
And it's about a 45 minute drive

00:00:38.473 --> 00:00:41.953
so he doesn't like anything
about this new situation.

00:00:41.953 --> 00:00:45.441
He screams the entire way to daycare

00:00:45.441 --> 00:00:46.490
(screaming)

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:47.908
and the entire way back.

00:00:47.908 --> 00:00:49.131
(screaming)

00:00:49.131 --> 00:00:51.601
So I'm sitting in an hour and a half's

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:54.643
worth of screaming every day.

00:00:54.643 --> 00:00:55.909
So cheers.

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:59.869
So tonight's topic, Are
You Ready to Have Kids?

00:00:59.869 --> 00:01:00.702
No.

00:01:00.702 --> 00:01:03.338
So there's obviously the standard,

00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:05.507
like, oh are you financially stable?

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:07.483
Are you emotionally stable?

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:08.316
Probably not.

00:01:08.316 --> 00:01:10.171
That's not what we're
going to go into tonight

00:01:10.171 --> 00:01:11.823
because, yeah that's important,

00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:13.422
But there are some other

00:01:13.422 --> 00:01:15.603
unspoken things that
nobody really talks about

00:01:15.603 --> 00:01:16.891
that you gotta know.

00:01:16.891 --> 00:01:17.982
So first,

00:01:17.982 --> 00:01:20.206
have you ever killed a cactus?

00:01:20.206 --> 00:01:23.160
Because cacti are very hard to kill,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.522
they only need to be
watered like once month.

00:01:25.522 --> 00:01:27.717
So if you have managed to kill one,

00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:30.449
you probably shouldn't have kids.

00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:33.123
But I have actually killed several cacti

00:01:33.123 --> 00:01:35.926
so I don't know if that's bad.

00:01:35.926 --> 00:01:38.753
Next, have you ever fallen
asleep while driving

00:01:38.753 --> 00:01:40.520
and not gotten into an accident?

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.204
'Cause raising kids is just as dangerous

00:01:43.204 --> 00:01:44.439
and you're expected to do it

00:01:44.439 --> 00:01:46.518
while constantly exhausted.

00:01:46.518 --> 00:01:48.615
There is a very special type of tired

00:01:48.615 --> 00:01:51.205
that you get to experience
once you've had kids.

00:01:51.205 --> 00:01:54.426
I have done the weirdest shit

00:01:54.426 --> 00:01:55.586
from lack of sleep.

00:01:55.586 --> 00:01:57.458
Like I'll go outside

00:01:57.458 --> 00:02:00.807
and see that I've given our dog a bottle.

00:02:00.807 --> 00:02:02.105
I've given her a bottle,

00:02:02.105 --> 00:02:04.298
I've given my kid dog food,

00:02:04.298 --> 00:02:06.445
no I have not given my kids dog food.

00:02:06.445 --> 00:02:08.676
Maybe they've eaten it a couple times.

00:02:08.676 --> 00:02:09.509
It's fine.

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:12.731
This rosé is kinda strong.

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:15.279
Can wines be stronger than others?

00:02:15.279 --> 00:02:18.772
Next, how strong are
the soles of your feet?

00:02:18.772 --> 00:02:22.379
'Cause you're about to be
walking on Legos everyday.

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:24.122
When my husband and I first got married

00:02:24.122 --> 00:02:25.619
he was very adamant about

00:02:25.619 --> 00:02:28.626
there are not going to be any kid toys

00:02:28.626 --> 00:02:30.285
anywhere but their rooms.

00:02:30.285 --> 00:02:32.502
And I was like, yeah, okay, sure buddy.

00:02:32.502 --> 00:02:33.335
Hey, hey,

00:02:34.831 --> 00:02:35.664
hey,

00:02:35.664 --> 00:02:36.497
hey.

00:02:36.497 --> 00:02:37.330
Everywhere.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.163
Hey.

00:02:38.163 --> 00:02:39.711
This is my living room right here.

00:02:39.711 --> 00:02:40.788
This shit.

00:02:40.788 --> 00:02:41.645
Next,

00:02:41.645 --> 00:02:44.331
do you like to schedule your own day?

00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:45.959
'Cause once you have kids,

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:49.376
your day is going to revolve around naps.

00:02:50.783 --> 00:02:53.829
If your child skips a nap,
they are no longer a child.

00:02:53.829 --> 00:02:56.455
They're suddenly a little gremlin

00:02:56.455 --> 00:02:58.216
and the more time that progresses,

00:02:58.216 --> 00:03:00.085
the more gremlin they become.

00:03:00.085 --> 00:03:01.983
So my four year old is at this stage

00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:04.117
where he thinks he
doesn't need naps anymore.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.897
After the time that he's missed it,

00:03:05.897 --> 00:03:07.600
it's always like 5 PM,

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:11.305
he just melts into this puddle of screech.

00:03:11.305 --> 00:03:12.876
(screeches)

00:03:12.876 --> 00:03:14.141
When my kids skip their naps,

00:03:14.141 --> 00:03:16.488
it is 6 PM mandatory bed time.

00:03:16.488 --> 00:03:17.634
Like no questions,

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.797
you get in bed and count some sheep

00:03:19.797 --> 00:03:21.085
even if you don't know how to count.

00:03:21.085 --> 00:03:22.487
Neither of my kids knows how to count

00:03:22.487 --> 00:03:23.646
but figure it out.

00:03:23.646 --> 00:03:25.070
Hold on.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.408
Hold on.

00:03:26.408 --> 00:03:28.503
Next, you're going to the bathroom,

00:03:28.503 --> 00:03:32.026
and your sunglasses
accidentally fall in the toilet

00:03:32.026 --> 00:03:33.254
do you pick them up?

00:03:33.254 --> 00:03:35.708
'Cause if you do, you're
probably ready for kids.

00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:37.058
Like this morning,

00:03:37.058 --> 00:03:38.962
my one and a half year old woke up.

00:03:38.962 --> 00:03:39.841
I like pick him up

00:03:39.841 --> 00:03:41.254
and I feel something kinda wet,

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.260
so I lay him down and I pull my arm up

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.727
and my arm was just like

00:03:45.727 --> 00:03:46.582
brown.

00:03:46.582 --> 00:03:48.214
It's shit.

00:03:48.214 --> 00:03:50.901
It has leaked out the back of his diaper

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.292
all onto his back

00:03:52.292 --> 00:03:53.536
and so when I picked him up,

00:03:53.536 --> 00:03:56.153
I just like squished it all over my arm.

00:03:56.153 --> 00:03:57.176
I don't even blink,

00:03:57.176 --> 00:03:59.173
I just take some wipes, wipe it off,

00:03:59.173 --> 00:04:00.602
get some sanitizer,

00:04:00.602 --> 00:04:02.648
rub it on, wash it off with soap.

00:04:02.648 --> 00:04:04.048
No harm, no foul.

00:04:04.048 --> 00:04:06.618
Just got shit all over my arm, who cares?

00:04:06.618 --> 00:04:08.589
I'm really enjoying this enamel glass

00:04:08.589 --> 00:04:10.755
because it doesn't show how much

00:04:10.755 --> 00:04:11.998
is being drank.

00:04:11.998 --> 00:04:13.506
You don't know if my glass is full,

00:04:13.506 --> 00:04:14.845
you don't know if it's empty.

00:04:14.845 --> 00:04:17.702
I could've only had
like two sips this time.

00:04:17.702 --> 00:04:19.200
So, how did you do?

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.799
I hope you were keeping score.

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:22.028
If you weren't keeping score,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.712
why the fuck are you watching this?

00:04:23.712 --> 00:04:25.070
You shouldn't say the F word.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.543
So how did you do?

00:04:26.543 --> 00:04:29.710
'Cause if you scored two out of three,

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:31.934
two out of 10.

00:04:33.751 --> 00:04:36.344
How many things did I even say?

00:04:36.344 --> 00:04:37.874
It doesn't even matter what your score is

00:04:37.874 --> 00:04:38.848
because to be honest,

00:04:38.848 --> 00:04:41.260
you could be all ready on paper,

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.753
nothing is gonna prepare you
for actually having kids.

00:04:44.753 --> 00:04:48.011
I read probably seven parenting books.

00:04:48.011 --> 00:04:49.127
Yeah, it's great,

00:04:49.127 --> 00:04:51.847
you need to cut your kid's grapes in half,

00:04:51.847 --> 00:04:53.921
that doesn't teach you how to deal with

00:04:53.921 --> 00:04:55.914
a certain child's temper tantrum.

00:04:55.914 --> 00:04:57.828
One of my son's likes to
be patted on the back.

00:04:57.828 --> 00:04:59.927
The other one likes to be held and rocked

00:04:59.927 --> 00:05:02.470
very very close, there's
no book on parenting

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:05.009
that's gonna teach you
how to parent your child.

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:06.176
So fuck books,

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.997
don't read.

00:05:08.997 --> 00:05:10.212
So that's it for now.

00:05:10.212 --> 00:05:12.839
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom

00:05:12.839 --> 00:05:14.860
and if there's anything
you want me to talk about,

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.007
leave it in the comments

00:05:16.007 --> 00:05:17.158
because I read them

00:05:17.158 --> 00:05:19.991
and I love to talk about what
you guys are interested in.

00:05:19.991 --> 00:05:23.371
And to all you people
about to comment saying,

00:05:23.371 --> 00:05:25.146
oh, this is why I never want kids,

00:05:25.146 --> 00:05:26.507
you will have kids.

00:05:26.507 --> 00:05:28.002
I was one of those people

00:05:28.002 --> 00:05:29.317
and now I have two.

00:05:29.317 --> 00:05:30.883
So until next time,

00:05:30.883 --> 00:05:33.310
go make some babies.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.143
Goodnight.

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:37.766
(burp)

00:05:38.657 --> 00:05:41.990
Gave you a burp, that's what I gave you.

